=== B. generator-less component (bus 5 of case9 islanded by removing lines 4-5, 5-6): J singular, algebraic equations inconsistent ===
lines removed: 2  smallest J eigenvalues: [6.92713769e-15 2.60600987e+00]  Pd at the isolated bus: 0.900 pu
residual g at isolated bus (cannot be removed by any theta, J row is zero): -0.9
=> the descriptor model is not index-1 there: Newton step is undefined, S does not exist; margin transfer has no meaning.

=== B2. islanding where every island keeps a generator (case9: remove lines 4-5 and 6-7 -> island {5,6,3} with generator 3): per-component Lemma 1 holds, but a shift of one island's rotors moves that island's angles ===
re-solved algebraic baseline on the islanded network: residual 6.661338147750939e-16  max line angle 8.8 deg
J min eig 1.971 ; min S entry 0.00e+00 ; max|rowsum-1| 3.3e-16 ; gain G=0.275 (<=1 per component holds)
shifting only gen 3 by 0.05 rad (a rotor-error span of 0.05 on the whole system, common-mode on that island): max change of ANY bus angle = 0.0500 rad; max change of any line/rotor-bus angle = 0.0000 rad (<= span 0.05)
common-mode shift of ALL rotors by 0.05: max change of constrained angles = 4.16e-17 (still zero: islands are shifted rigidly each)

